--TEST--
a legacy cast does not parse, so the cursor is on no symbol and renaming there is refused, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
int $n = 3;
int $m = (i<|>nt)$n;
--REQUEST--
rename to=count
--EXPECT--
refused: There is nothing to rename here. You can rename a class, a variable, a method, a property, a constant or an enum case.
